  ],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The key structural change in the solid granny is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "into-the-top"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "working into the cluster top"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " on the side positions instead of into a chain space — there is no chain-1 between side "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-cluster"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble clusters"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Only the corners keep their chain-2 spaces. The result is heavier than a standard granny with noticeably less drape — better suited for bags, pot holders, and structured panel work than for blankets. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " closes the centre. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with steam sharpens the corners on dense fabric."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 30 m per square. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "10 × 10 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook, steam-blocked. The solid construction is denser than an open granny of the same round count — a four-round solid granny is the approximate size of a three-round open granny."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3-treble cluster (3tr cl)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first tr throughout. Corners: (3tr cl, ch 2, 3tr cl). Side clusters in rounds 2 onward are worked directly into the top of the previous cluster — no chain between them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr, ch 2. *(3 tr, ch 2); repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. Pull tail. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corners)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. *3 tr into the top of the next cluster (no chain between). (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp; repeat from * 2 more times. 3 tr into the top of last cluster. Sl st to top of ch-3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, no side ch sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. *3 tr into top of each side cluster (2 clusters per side), no chains between. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp; repeat from * 2 more times. Complete last side. Sl st to top of ch-3. (36 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, no side ch sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. *3 tr into top of each side cluster (3 clusters per side), no chains between. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp; repeat from * 2 more times. Complete last side. Sl st to top of ch-3. Fasten off. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, no side ch sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Steam-block to 10 × 10 cm using a damp cloth and moderate steam. The dense fabric holds its shape well without pinning, but pinning at the corners gives sharper right angles."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join with the flat slip-stitch method, working through the cluster tops along each side. The absence of chain spaces makes the seam tighter than on an open granny — use the same hook size throughout."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 40 degrees. The dense fabric is robust. Reshape while damp and dry flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use the solid granny construction for a market bag by joining four squares into a flat panel and then folding and seaming. The density holds shape under load in a way that open granny squares cannot. For a visual contrast, work the corner chain-2 spaces in a contrast colour by joining a new yarn at the start of each corner sp."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}